    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27209" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŭo</span></b> , lui, 3, v. a.
		root lu-, to wash; Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λούω,
			λουτρόν</span>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῦμα,
			λύθρον</span>, polluo, diluo, and lavo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to wash,
				lave.</i>—<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Graecia luitur Ionio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					11, 22</span></i>
			: amnis moenia luit, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 3, 190.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to cleanse,
			purge</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insontes errore luit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 3, 407</span></i>
			.</div>
